# K03 S6 (Codex K03-CALLABLE-PATH-20261007-25, answer (c); docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption,
# #callables): a path that selects a callable, written alone as a statement, is that callable's nullary call, as
# `Holder\tick()` is -- Holder's field `fn: tick` refers to the unit's tick (Q22, LMX_blog/q/q22.md).  Selecting tick
# runs nothing of Holder: its own statement `bump()` would count a run.  tick runs twice, Holder never: exit 7; 81 if
# Holder ran, 82 a wrong count of tick.
int: hits 0
int: seen 0
fn: tick () int
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
    return: node\hits
end: tick
fn: bump () int
    node\seen: node\seen + 1
    return: 0
end: bump
fn: count () int
    return: node\hits
end: count
fn: saw () int
    return: node\seen
end: saw
Holder:
    fn: tick
    bump()
end: Holder
fn: run () int
    Holder\tick
    Holder\tick()
    if: saw() != 0
        return: 81
    if: count() != 2
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: run
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: run(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
